878	  // (scsi1+, `vmdata:vm-<vmid>-disk-N`). A disk named `vm-<vmid>-disk-N` is owned
879	  // by that vmid, and both purge and the default destroy (which removes disks
880	  // referenced in config, incl. detached `unusedN` entries) delete it; there is no
881	  // Proxmox API to selectively spare it, and the reinstall re-clones onto the SAME
882	  // vmid, so we cannot GUARANTEE such a disk survives the destroy. Rather than risk
